# openOODA/INDEX — The Polyrepo

File: openOODA/docs/INDEX.oot

This file is the overview of the openOODA project as a whole. It is the
front-door copy for human visitors; the agent-facing front door is at
`openOODA/ANCHOR.oot`.

## 1. What it is

The openOODA polyrepo. Nine independent repositories that together form
a sovereign, capability-secure systems language for the AI era. One
`.oo` source compiles to four native targets. Every effect requires an
explicit capability token. The standard library has zero ambient
authority. Each repo owns its own surface, version, and release; the
goal is to make them as independent of each other as possible while
remaining functionally aligned.

The repositories cooperate through a single `ooda` binary and a content-
addressed package registry. The compiler is the substrate; the standard
library, package manager, CLI driver, language server, MCP server, and
runtime are siblings, not dependencies.

## 2. Surface

The nine polyrepo repos (as of 2026-09-03):

| Repo        | Role                                                   | Status      |
|-------------|--------------------------------------------------------|-------------|
| `openOODA/` | Governance: rules, north star, RFCs, polyrepo topology | v1.0.7      |
| `ooda/`     | Legacy monorepo (will be killed when oodac/oodar fully replace it) | deprecated |
| `std/`      | Standard library: 8 functional domains, 173 modules     | v1.0.3      |
| `opm/`      | Package manager: CAS-by-sha, capability-tagged         | v0.8.x      |
| `ooda/`     | The `ooda` binary driver, 13 subcommands                | v0.2.1      |
| `lsp/`      | Language server: 16 methods, 5 editor integrations     | v0.6.2      |
| `mcp/`      | MCP server: 23 tools, 5 tiers                          | v0.6.x      |
| `oodar/`    | Gen 1 C host substrate: 30 capability tokens, Landlock, arena, PQC, 6-subdir layout (core/sec/fs/net/hw/app) | v2.0.0 |
| `oodac/`    | Compiler (extracted from `ooda/`; gemini v0.1.x reorg + cap-ABI alignment) | v0.1.x |

## 3. Where to go next

- **The submenu.** Each repo has its own page sourced from its
  `openOODA/{repo}/docs/` directory.
- **The 14 capability tokens.** They appear across the LSP, MCP, and
  std visualisations. There is no ambient authority anywhere in the
  stack.
- **The polyrepo topology.** See `openOODA/RULES.oot` §1.23 for the
  why behind the split.

> The install command lives at the top and bottom of this page —
> it is the same component, not duplicated content.
